-  <HaulersDream.Setting.HaulTamedSlaughter>Haul slaughtered carcasses to storage</HaulersDream.Setting.HaulTamedSlaughter>
-  <HaulersDream.Setting.HaulTamedSlaughterDesc>When a colonist finishes slaughtering a colony animal, the fresh carcass is hauled straight to storage (a freezer or corpse stockpile) so it doesn't rot where it fell — only if a reachable storage spot accepts it, otherwise it's left exactly as vanilla. (Vanilla never hauls a slaughtered animal itself; this closes that gap.)</HaulersDream.Setting.HaulTamedSlaughterDesc>
-  <HaulersDream.Setting.HaulWildKills>Haul hunted carcasses to storage</HaulersDream.Setting.HaulWildKills>
-  <HaulersDream.Setting.HaulWildKillsDesc>When a hunt is interrupted right after the kill — the hunter is pulled away by a need, a draft, a mental break, or the hunt times out — the hunter promptly hauls the fresh carcass to storage on its way out, instead of leaving it for the slow general haul queue. On a clean hunt the hunter already carries its kill home (vanilla), so this stays out of the way — no double-hauling. Only hauls if a reachable storage spot accepts the body; otherwise the carcass is left exactly as vanilla (it's never forbidden, so normal corpse hauling still collects it once a freezer or corpse stockpile that accepts it exists).</HaulersDream.Setting.HaulWildKillsDesc>
+  <HaulersDream.Setting.HaulTamedSlaughter>Haul colony-animal carcasses to storage</HaulersDream.Setting.HaulTamedSlaughter>
+  <HaulersDream.Setting.HaulTamedSlaughterDesc>After slaughtering a colony animal, or finishing it off with Allow Tool (when it permits the target), an eligible pawn adds a carcass haul after its existing queued orders. Requires an allowed carcass and reachable storage that accepts it. Does not un-forbid the carcass or replace queued work.</HaulersDream.Setting.HaulTamedSlaughterDesc>
+  <HaulersDream.Setting.HaulWildKills>Haul wild-animal carcasses to storage</HaulersDream.Setting.HaulWildKills>
+  <HaulersDream.Setting.HaulWildKillsDesc>After an interrupted hunt that killed its prey, or finishing off a factionless wild animal with Allow Tool or Keyz' Allow Utilities, an eligible pawn adds a carcass haul after its existing queued orders. Requires an allowed carcass and reachable storage that accepts it; never un-forbids the carcass. A completed vanilla hunt keeps its own hauling, without an extra haul.</HaulersDream.Setting.HaulWildKillsDesc>
 
   <HaulersDream.Setting.ButcherSpoilingFirst>Butcher the most-spoiled corpse first</HaulersDream.Setting.ButcherSpoilingFirst>
   <HaulersDream.Setting.ButcherSpoilingFirstDesc>When a colonist picks a corpse for a butcher bill, they choose the body closest to rotting (among the corpses the bill already allows, within its ingredient search radius) instead of just the nearest — so meat is recovered before it spoils. Only reorders which already-valid corpse is used; never changes the recipe, the search radius, or which corpses the bill accepts. Frozen corpses are left for last (they aren't spoiling). Applies to both ordinary butcher bills and Hauler's Dream batches. On by default.</HaulersDream.Setting.ButcherSpoilingFirstDesc>
